It's just another new choice, and not IMO a terribly unbalancing one.
Magical breathing is one way to cross water, the other two being
levitation and water walking.  (Of course you can also freeze it or
fill it in.)  With a diving helmet, you save one footwear, amulet or
ring slot, but use up your headgear slot.  And since it's a metal
helmet, your spellcasting will suffer -- it's definitely not likely to
be a good choice for wizards, or for spellcasters in general.

As to its properties, real old-fashioned diving helmets were pretty
heavy.  The weight should probably be somewhere between 50 and 100:
heavier than an ordinary helmet but not so heavy as to make it utterly
impractical.  It should probably also protect against certain types of
blinding the way lenses and visored helmets (I think) do.

The un-ID'd appearance could be "a spherical helmet".

